<p style="opacity:.6;font-size:12px;max-width:130ch">Diskbox replaces the Disk Viewer tile. The array is shown as one card with a parity row underneath: green when the array is protected, amber while a parity check or rebuild runs, red when there is no protection, a data disk is emulated, or a disk has failed. The Needs attention list collects disks that are too full, too hot, show SMART warnings or are in a bad state.</p>

<p style="opacity:.6;font-size:12px;max-width:130ch">Temperature limits for SSDs and NVMe devices are taken from Unraid's own display settings (Settings, Display Settings). SMART data is collected every 20 minutes with <code>smartctl</code>; disks that are spun down are skipped, so Diskbox never wakes a sleeping disk. Utilization and temperature colours use the values above, or Unraid's own when a field is empty.</p>

<p style="opacity:.6;font-size:12px;max-width:130ch">Discord alerts: Unraid checks every minute and posts to the webhook only when something changes: a problem appears, gets worse, or is over. A temperature alert needs three minutes in a row and an all-clear only after the disk has cooled two degrees; red alerts can repeat after the chosen number of hours. A SMART warning can be acknowledged with the button next to it on the dashboard tile; it then counts again only when it gets worse (the attribute's raw value rises). A failed health check cannot be acknowledged. SMART alerts name each attribute, say whether it is Pre-fail or Old age, and show its raw value, its previous value, and the value, worst and threshold. The buttons use the saved settings, so press Apply first. Create a webhook in Discord under channel settings, Integrations, Webhooks.</p>

<script>
$(function () {
  var $tm = $('#dbx-tmsg');
  $.each({test: '#dbx-test', sample: '#dbx-sample', weekly: '#dbx-weekly'}, function (op, sel) {
    $(sel).on('click', function () {
      var $b = $(this).prop('disabled', true);
      $tm.css('color', '').text('Sending...');
      $.post('/plugins/diskbox/test.php', {op: op}, null, 'json')
        .done(function (r) { if (r && r.ok) { $tm.css('color', '#3fa24a').text('Sent.'); } else { $tm.css('color', '#e5534b').text('Not sent: ' + ((r && r.error) ? r.error : 'unknown error')); } })
        .fail(function (x) { var e = (x.responseJSON && x.responseJSON.error) ? x.responseJSON.error : 'HTTP ' + x.status; $tm.css('color', '#e5534b').text('Not sent: ' + e); })
        .always(function () { $b.prop('disabled', false); });
    });
  });
  $('.dbx-forget').on('click', function () {
    var $b = $(this).prop('disabled', true);
    $.post('/plugins/diskbox/ack.php', { name: $b.data('disk'), op: 'forget' }, null, 'json').always(function () { $b.closest('dd').prev('dt').remove(); $b.closest('dd').text('forgotten: a warning on this disk counts again'); });
  });
  var $msg = $('#dbx-msg');
  $('#dbx-save').on('click', function () {
    var $b = $(this).prop('disabled', true);
    $msg.css('color', '').text('Saving...');
    $.post('/plugins/diskbox/save.php', $('#dbx-form').serialize(), null, 'json')
      .done(function (r) {
        if (r && r.ok) {
          $msg.css('color', '#3fa24a').text('Saved. The dashboard picks it up within a few seconds.');
        } else {
          $msg.css('color', '#e5534b').text('Not saved: ' + ((r && r.error) ? r.error : 'unknown error'));
        }
      })
      .fail(function (x) {
        var e = (x.responseJSON && x.responseJSON.error) ? x.responseJSON.error : 'HTTP ' + x.status;
        $msg.css('color', '#e5534b').text('Not saved: ' + e);
      })
      .always(function () { $b.prop('disabled', false); });
  });
});
</script>
